# Reel Estate → ComfyUI: Complete Feature Replication Guide

Based on my research of tryreelestate.com, here is every feature they offer, mapped to exactly what you can and cannot do with LTX Video + what you need to add to ComfyUI to achieve full parity.

---

## 🗂️ Complete Feature List from Reel Estate

Reel Estate's core feature set breaks down into **6 functional pillars**:

1. Image-to-Video clip generation (with cinematic motion)
2. AI Virtual Staging (furnishing empty rooms)
3. Photo Effects (Twilight, Winter, Christmas, Halloween, etc.)
4. Restage & Refine (multiple versions of same photo)
5. Video Assembly (timeline, clip ordering, duration control)
6. Export & Watermarking (MP4, 720p/1080p, portrait/landscape, custom watermark, background music)

---

## ✅ What LTX Video Already Covers

**LTX Video (LTX-Video by Lightricks)** is a strong image-to-video model. Here's what it natively handles:

| Reel Estate Feature | LTX Coverage | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Image → animated video clip | ✅ Full | Core strength of LTX — smooth, cinematic motion from still photos |
| Cinematic camera motion | ✅ Good | Pan, zoom, push, pull via prompt conditioning or motion guidance nodes |
| Portrait & Landscape format | ✅ Full | Control via resolution settings in the KSampler/LTX node (e.g., 768x1360 vs 1360x768) |
| Clip reuse (generate once, reuse) | ✅ Full | Once rendered in ComfyUI, the MP4 clip is yours forever |
| Multi-image batch processing | ✅ Full | Loop nodes in ComfyUI can batch all listing photos through LTX |
| HD output (1080p) | ✅ Full | LTX supports up to 1216x704 natively; upscale workflow handles 1080p |

